cast:
  Will:
  Zofia:
  Doyle:
  Grace:
~~~~
accusation
----------
Zofia: The date. It says “this week”, not 1666. The Witness Workshop. Never heard of them.
Grace: Nobody has.
Zofia: Their new teaching sheet: “The bakery deliberately started the Fire.” Did you know they were saying that?
Will: Deliberately? Master would sooner burn his own hands than waste a batch. Who has set that down? [class=dead]
Zofia: No author on this side. An editor's address on the back.
Will: Then write there. Have it taken off. Every word. [class=dead]
Zofia: What did you see?
Will: I worked there. There was flour to weigh and bread to count. A man does not feed a street in order to burn it. [class=dead]
Zofia: That's a reason to doubt the sentence. It isn't something you saw.
Will: There were men saying foreigners had fired the houses. They would not all have said it without cause. [class=dead]
Zofia: Saying it again doesn't prove it. A foreign name isn't evidence of setting a fire.
Will: You ask what I heard, then stop your ears to the men in the street. [class=dead]
Zofia: Who said it? Names. Had they seen anyone light anything?
Will: In the street. I did not take their names. There was other work. [class=dead]
Zofia: You want me to write to an editor with that? I'll find something I can send. No promises.
Will: There was a delivery. Weighed before it went out. I remember that plainly enough. [class=dead]
Zofia: How much?
Will: First write that Master did not start it. [class=dead]
Zofia: I can't buy a quantity with a conclusion.
Will: Nor can I give you flour to put in another man's loaf. [class=dead]
Will: Put that I asked you to strike it out. [class=dead]
Zofia: I'll put that you asked.

plaque
------
Zofia: The green plaque. It says “worked and wrote his stories here in 1891”. Nothing about dying here.
Doyle: My dear, have you come about the practice, or have you brought a case? [class=dead]
Zofia: A boy. And this caption from the same Workshop. Dated this week: “Arthur Conan Doyle: Holmes and nothing else.”
Doyle: Nothing else is a considerable deletion. My spiritualist writing alone should prevent it. Have they found it inconvenient? [class=dead]
Zofia: You didn't know about the caption?
Doyle: Until you read it, no. I should like the omission corrected. They may disagree with a book without pretending it was never written. [class=dead]
Zofia: Holmes, there's a boy at the Monument who—
Doyle: Doyle. If you employ my detective, you must expect his author to remain unemployed. [class=dead]
Zofia: Sorry. I need someone who can test a statement without deciding the answer first.
Doyle: Then begin with the evidence. Consider the Cottingley photographs: an image offers something more substantial than a rumour. I regarded those photographs as evidence of fairies. [class=dead]
Zofia: They were shown to be fakes. That’s in the account I brought. Look—here.
Doyle: An unwelcome sequel, my dear. Will you strike out the books as well as the fairies? [class=dead]
Zofia: No. You wrote them. Getting the pictures wrong doesn't unwrite a book.
Doyle: Then date this unpleasant sequel, if you please. I have learned it from you today; I shall not pretend I knew it all along. [class=dead]
Zofia: Today. You heard about both today. Will you come with me to question the boy?
Doyle: An invitation to inquiry. I should have preferred lunch. [class=dead]
Zofia: I have a sandwich.
Doyle: You will have to eat it. I foresee a defect in this arrangement. [class=dead]

otherwork
---------
Zofia: Before we go: this heading says “Sir Arthur Conan Doyle”. The caption leaves room for a title, but not for another book.
Doyle: Ask it to accommodate Professor Challenger. The Lost World appeared in 1912. There are historical novels as well as detective stories, and the spiritualist work you have already mentioned. [class=dead]
Zofia: I'll put those in the request. What about the title? The sheet makes it look like a prize for Holmes.
Doyle: I was knighted in 1902. I believed the reason was my pamphlet defending Britain's conduct in the Boer War. I did not understand it as a reward for Holmes. [class=dead]
Zofia: So I can't just write “knighted for the pamphlet” either?
Doyle: My dear, I should be delighted to settle the matter myself. But you have my understanding of it; do check me. [class=dead]
Zofia: Your medical training might help with Will. He counts what went into a bakery. We need to ask what the quantities can actually tell us.
Doyle: I graduated in medicine at the University of Edinburgh in 1881. Joseph Bell, my teacher, helped inspire Holmes: close attention to particulars can disturb an attractive first impression. [class=dead]
Zofia: Born in Edinburgh too? This caption doesn't get you out of London.
Doyle: Indeed, my dear; London must spare me a birthplace. Now, what does your boy actually want corrected? [class=dead]
Zofia: “Deliberately.” But he wants me to take out “bakery” as well.
Doyle: A large favour concealed inside a small correction. Let us hear him, my dear. [class=dead]

climb
-----
Grace: Are we paying to go upstairs because a boy I can't hear won't answer a question downstairs?
Zofia: He says he'll talk on the way. You can stay here. I said I'd be back with you; I didn't book your whole afternoon.
Grace: I'll come. But if he changes the destination at the top, we are coming down.
Will: We pay to climb it? After the shop burned? [class=dead]
Zofia: He objects to the price.
Grace: At last, something we can all discuss.
Will: For that money, ought there not to be bread? [class=dead]
Zofia: He would like bread included.
Grace: Tell him to ask the person who thought “stairs” was a complete visitor experience.
Zofia: Gallery, 202 feet. Nearly there?
Grace: That's the whole column. The gallery’s below the top. And it says 311 steps. Keep going.
Zofia: Height equals distance to Pudding Lane. We climb all this and the bakery's only that far away?
Grace: Sir Christopher Wren and Dr Robert Hooke designed it. Built from 1671 to 1677. Six years. Why do we still do this—climb all the way up to remember a fire?
Zofia: Grace wants to know why we're climbing.
Will: I would see where the shop stood. Those houses block it from below. [class=dead]
Zofia: He wants to see where the shop was.
Grace: It commemorates the Fire and the rebuilding of the City. We paid for everyone’s stairs, then.
Will: All that stone, and no place in it for a sack to stay dry. [class=dead]
Zofia: You couldn't have seen it built. It came after your death. Do you know why you're here?
Will: I know where I may stand. I know you can hear me. I cannot account for the masons. [class=dead]
Zofia: Fine. But I'm asking about the delivery at the top.
Grace: Can we stop for a moment? Somebody has been talking instead of breathing.
Zofia: Me. The others don't need to.
Grace: Excellent. They can wait while we do.

origin
------
Zofia: This sheet names Farriner’s bakery. Same door?
Will: Then you have brought their charge back up the stairs. [class=dead]
Zofia: The place it began. That doesn't prove someone there deliberately lit it. Look—‘deliberately’ is only on the Workshop sheet.
Will: What of the foreigners? I heard it before I died. You cannot say I heard nothing. [class=dead]
Zofia: Wait. Robert Hubert. French watchmaker. He confessed—
Doyle: You have stopped reading, my dear. What follows the confession? [class=dead]
Zofia: It was false. He was hanged at Tyburn on 27 October 1666. The evidence puts him at sea when the Fire started. He only arrived two days afterwards.
Will: He confessed to a thing he could not have done? [class=dead]
Zofia: Yes. A confession still needed testing. His being French did not fill the gap.
Doyle: A most obliging culprit, my dear—until one asks where he was. Your street has supplied a rumour; it has not supplied a man who could have done it. [class=dead]
Grace: And are you going to make the sheet say that, or just make your own notes better?
Zofia: I'm sending them ‘deliberately’. Let them show us where they got it.
Will: I cannot weigh their tale. But write “not the bakery”. That much you can give Master. [class=dead]
Zofia: I can't. The bakery remains the starting place.
Will: You will leave his door marked. [class=dead]
Zofia: I won't write that he chose to burn London. I can't take his door out of the street.
Grace: You've gone quiet. What is he asking you to change?
Zofia: ‘Not the bakery’. Still. Like I can rub the address off.
Grace: And if he won't?
Zofia: I send what I can support. Without his delivery quantity.
Will: You would use less than a full measure? [class=dead]
Zofia: There'll be a blank where your weight should be. I'm sending it anyway.

carving
-------
Will: What do the words on the stone say of Master? [class=dead]
Zofia: There's a translation on my phone. A later bit blames Catholics. Added in 1681.
Will: They cut a street tale into stone? Fifteen years to sharpen the chisel? [class=dead]
Zofia: Taken off under James II in 1685. Put back in 1689. Chiselled out for good in 1830.
Doyle: Back again? My dear, give us the dates with the words. I should like to know which edition of this stone we are consulting. [class=dead]
Grace: Does your publisher even know its own sentence is an accusation?
Zofia: I'll send them their exact words. They can hardly say they haven't seen them.
Will: They laid new bricks. Was there no man left to count what burned? [class=dead]
Zofia: New streets, new St Paul's. You'd think somebody would have sorted it out.
Will: A new oven does not count yesterday's loaves. [class=dead]
Zofia: I'll borrow that. With your name on it.
Grace: Send the request before you make him editor.
